      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head>App AGu 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="App AGu 4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="394" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis recedat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.28"/> a domino suo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.27"/> sine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.9"/> licentia (preter licentiam) uel in aliam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.9"/> schiram (alium comitatum) se subducat, et inquiratur (ubi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.29"/> sit), redeat ubi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.30"/> prius fuit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.31"/>, et emendet domino suo LX sol.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="394" ed="#liebermann"/>4. Wenn jemand von seinem Herrn ohne Erlaubniss fortzieht oder in einen anderen Amtsbezirk sich fortstiehlt und erkundet wird, (wo er ist <hi rend="italic">Qu. II</hi>), kehre er zurück [dorthin], wo er früher war, und büsse seinem Herrn 60 Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">4. If anyone departs from his lord without permission or steals away into another official district and is discovered, (where he is <hi rend="italic">Qu. II</hi>), let him return [to the place] where he was before, and pay his lord 60 shill. compensation.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="394"><ref target="clause:Ine_39">Ine 39</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 39</note>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text and German translation transcribed from Gesetze I p. 394 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page); Liebermann prints in smaller type: Wenn jemand von seinem Herrn ohne Erlaubniss fortzieht oder in einen anderen Amtsbezirk sich fortstiehlt und erkundet wird, | kehre er zurück [dorthin], wo er früher war, und | seinem Herrn 60 Schill.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor der Klammer Lond, eingeklammertes übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the text before the brackets Lond; the bracketed text the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so KCo;</hi> -dit <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus KCo; -dit the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. s. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. s. omitted in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ut <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ut Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="App-AGu_4.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">394</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sit <hi rend="italic">HkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sit HkBr</seg></note>
